From: Scott Jordan <scott@spaceshipcreative.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:15:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10/25] List FLASHINFER_MLA_SPARSE_SM90 after SM120 on
 capability 12

Source: MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-NVFP4-Dual-DGX-Spark,
  glm53-flash_SM121.py, step bake_sm90_on_capability_12 (MIT,
  Copyright (c) 2026 MiaAI-Lab), via the copy vendored in
  kindlingai/glm-5.3-flash-gx10 image/patches/ at c748079. The anchor
  matched v0.31.0 once. Retargeted: MiaAI puts SM90 ahead of SM120; this
  puts it after.
Upstream status: absent.

MiaAI's patch inserts FLASHINFER_MLA_SPARSE_SM90 before
FLASHINFER_MLA_SPARSE_SM120 in the capability-12 MLA priorities, making
the FA2 path the default on GB10. Here it goes last instead, so:

- no configuration that selects SM120 today changes. Sparse-MLA models
  on RTX 50xx / RTX PRO (head 576) keep SM120 and fp8_ds_mla, and a
  stock FlashInfer, which cannot run FA2 with fp8 KV on SM12x, is never
  chosen implicitly;
- SM90 is auto-selected only where SM120 rejects the config, for example
  --kv-cache-dtype bfloat16 or a --block-size outside SM120's {64, 256},
  which today fails with "No valid attention backend";
- the GB10 recipe opts in explicitly:
    --attention-backend FLASHINFER_MLA_SPARSE_SM90 --kv-cache-dtype fp8
  and the A/B baseline stays one flag away:
    --attention-backend FLASHINFER_MLA_SPARSE_SM120

Explicit --attention-backend selection does not consult this list; the
list only affects auto-selection.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 vllm/platforms/cuda.py | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/vllm/platforms/cuda.py b/vllm/platforms/cuda.py
index ba333d53f..c1636d793 100644
--- a/vllm/platforms/cuda.py
+++ b/vllm/platforms/cuda.py
@@ -133,6 +133,10 @@ def _get_backend_priorities(
             return [
                 AttentionBackendEnum.TRITON_MLA,
                 AttentionBackendEnum.FLASHINFER_MLA_SPARSE_SM120,
+                # FA2 on SM12x. Only auto-selected where SM120 rejects the
+                # config (e.g. a bf16 KV cache); otherwise opt in with
+                # --attention-backend FLASHINFER_MLA_SPARSE_SM90.
+                AttentionBackendEnum.FLASHINFER_MLA_SPARSE_SM90,
             ]
         else:
             sparse_tail = [
